  "title": "Coast Guard Helicopter Crew Rescues Man From Saginaw Bay",
  "description": "A rescue swimmer, from a rescue helicopter crew aboard an MH-65C Dolphin helicopter from Coast Guard Air Station Detroit, is lowered down to the ice covering Saginaw Bay in the vicinity of Fish Point, Mich., to rescue one of two men who had fallen through the ice, March 2, 2013. After an overnight search, the Coast Guard called off the search for the other man who had fallen through the ice when their airboat capsized. U.S. Coast Guard video courtesy of Air Station Detroit.",
